{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>You are El Ro'i.</b> The sage Rabbi Abraham explained: 'You are a El who reveals Himself,' for the word ראי is a noun." "<b>Have I even here seen.</b> The meaning is: 'Have I even here seen' the angel of HaShem, after I had seen HaShem in my affliction."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {0 "'The sage Rabbi Abraham' refers to R. Abraham ibn Ezra.", 1 "The lemma is the continuation of the verse (Genesis 16:13); abbreviations השי\"ת and הש\"י both resolve to HaShem; the second occurrence printed הש\"י likely for הקב\"ה or הש\"י."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:12:46.036120342Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}